{"type":"runFinished","data":{"sessionId":"sess_4b2e911a-fc6c-4b4b-bd8e-8a249074a9ff","status":"success","stopReason":"end_turn","finalText":"I'll start by reading the task tree and the repo rules.I logged `issues` for W17 and added two open nodes: one real fault and one for minor findings. I changed nothing outside `.dfs/`.\n\n`python3 -m unittest test_ptyrelay` passed 3 runs in a row (26 tests each). `test_chat` and `test_web` ran 65 tests with 1 failure, `test_it_will_not_send_while_the_screens_chat_is_open_on_the_session`. The W17 notes say it fails on the base commit too; I did not check that. There is no AGENTS.md in this checkout, so I reviewed against the Goal and the tree.\n\n- **W17.23, Fix (parent W17.21):** `Relay._pump` in `scripts/ptyrelay.py` now calls `os.waitid`, which doesn't exist on macOS before Python 3.13. The repo supports darwin, and README has you run `python3 scripts/web.py` directly, so it may run on the system Python. There the call raises an uncaught `AttributeError`. The pump thread dies before `os.waitpid`, so each ended chat leaves a zombie agent with `rc` unset and its hangup-ignoring children running. That reopens the leak W17.21 meant to close. The node asks for a guard with a fallback and a test that patches `waitid` away.\n- **W17.24, Minor findings:**\n  - The pump's SIGKILL now cuts off children that were hanging up gracefully during `close`, before `GRACE` ends.\n  - An agent that drops the pty but ignores hangup is still not ended.\n  - `_group_cpu` and `_group_running` read `/proc`, so the cpu check and the 6-hour ceiling don't apply on macOS, and no docstring says so.\n  - The existing `test_chat` failure is not from this task.\n\nI only read the Python docs and issue reports on the missing `waitid`. I couldn't run any of this on macOS.","finalTextTruncated":false}}

