{"type":"runFinished","data":{"sessionId":"sess_1ff443b8-bc10-4a29-bbc3-e2fb0d5a351d","status":"success","stopReason":"end_turn","finalText":"Verdict logged: `ok`. I added no nodes and raised nothing.\n\nI couldn't run the map tests here. This box has no Python or Playwright environment, so I judged the changes by reading the code and tests. Nothing in them shows the Goal unmet:\n- **Labels:** a label that would overlap now takes a free place beside its object, and the greenhouse label shows at the whole-farm view.\n- **Zone taps:** a tap within a fingertip of a zone's outline opens that zone, and devices still win over zones.\n- **Box zoom:** the \"Zoom to an area\" tool is in place, and Escape mid-drag no longer lets the box reappear.\n- **Editor:** the tool is off in the editor and still off when you close it, and W132.11's new test covers that.\n\nThe task file I was given shows W132.11 as open because its Determination was stripped. Its commit a1c8299 is marked confirmed, so I took it as done.\n\nMinor findings, logged in the verdict body:\n- W132.11's new editor test stays green if only the `!edit` guard in the `pointerdown` handler is removed. That guard is untested defence.\n- A box drag under 12 px in either direction does nothing and leaves the tool on, with no cue.\n- The greenhouse label sits beside its zone with no leader line or other cue tying it to the zone.\n- W132.10 dropped the switched-off-layer guard on a Chromium-only probe. The CSS reads as safe in other browsers, but I didn't run it on Safari or Firefox.","finalTextTruncated":false}}

