list.I logged the verdict `ok` for W17: I found no gap against the Goal, so I added no nodes and raised nothing. I changed no code, and the working tree outside `.dfs/` is untouched.\n\n- **Goal coverage:** Ending a chat now ends the whole process group on every path I read. That covers New chat, close_all, the idle close and an agent that exits by itself, plus a page turn that times out, finishes, or has its server stopped, exits, or gets SIGTERM or SIGHUP. The setsid escape and the guessed idle times are already carried by the Hypotheses on W17.13, W17.14, W17.17 and W17.19, so I did not repeat them.\n- **Tests:** `test_ptyrelay` passed in two runs (26 tests). `test_chat` has one failure, `test_it_will_not_send_while_the_screens_chat_is_open_on_the_session`, which also fails on the base commit.\n- **Not run:** I did not run `test_screen`, which needs a terminal, or any real agent.\n\nMinor findings, as logged for the author:\n- **macOS Python version:** `_pump` in `scripts/ptyrelay.py` uses `os.waitid` with `WNOWAIT`, which exists on macOS only from Python 3.13. `flake.nix` lists darwin systems and takes `python3` from nixpkgs. I did not check which version the pinned nixpkgs gives; on an older one the pump thread dies without reaping the agent.\n- **Agent closes the pty but keeps running:** the relay is no longer live, so close and close_all skip it. Quitting the screen then leaves that agent running. I did not see this shape with any agent.\n- **Weak SIGTERM/SIGHUP screen test:** the screen's test only checks that `tui.main`'s source contains `exit_on_signals()`. It would still pass if the call moved somewhere that never runs. The web-server tests run a real process.\n- **Old failing test:** `test_it_will_not_send_while_the_screens_chat_is_open_on_the_session` is the one named above; `test_screen` needing a terminal is not from this task either.\n- **Unused return value:** `ChatHost.close` returns its reaper thread, but `UiWalker.chat_close` drops it. That is harmless because close_all joins the kept list.","finalTextTruncated":false}}

