tus":"success","stopReason":"end_turn","finalText":"I'll start by reading the task file and the commits since 2026-11-04.I logged the review verdict `ok` and added no nodes, because I found no fault a user would meet. I did not run the tests: the Python environment path that W132.11 names doesn't exist in this box, so I read the code and tests instead. The working tree outside `.dfs/` is unchanged.\n\nAgainst the Goal:\n- **Labels:** `declutter()` now tries free places around an object and hides a label only when none is free, so the greenhouse label shows at the whole-farm view.\n- **Small zone selection:** a tap within a fingertip of a zone's outline opens the zone, and devices still win over zones.\n- **Box zoom:** the tool is one-shot, Escape cancels it even mid-drag without the box coming back, and it is off in the editor.\n- **Assumptions:** plan labels, and the box zoom's one-shot, pointer-only and no-editor choices, each carry a Hypothesis with an answer page. I found no unmarked one.\n\nThe minor findings, logged in the verdict body:\n- **W132.11 status:** it is still `Status: started` in `W132.md` although its Determination is written and its commit message says confirmed. W132.6 and W132.8 had the same slip. It needs setting to confirmed.\n- **Hit rect:** a label moved off its home spot keeps its `.hit` rect under the icon. Real taps go through `nearestMarker()`, so only the fallback hit test is affected.\n- **Armed tool:** every tap, including on a device or zone, is swallowed while the box tool is armed. A drag of 12 px or more in one direction but under 12 px in the other also does nothing. The README says only that a tap or a drag under 12 px leaves the tool on.\n- **Fit button:** the ⤢ button also turns the box tool off, and the README doesn't say so.\n- **Stray attribute:** the box button's svg has a no-op `stroke-dasharray=\"none\"` on its corner path.\n- **Label cue:** the greenhouse label shown beside its zone has no cue tying it to the zone. Act on this only if the author finds it unclear.","finalTextTruncated":false}}

